 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios SpaceX and Tesla shares both fell more than 3% yesterday, and are in the red again this morning, as investors gauge the impact of midterm elections on Elon Musk's empire.

 Particular focus is on Texas, where Musk spent hundreds of millions of dollars in a failed effort to keep his adopted state red. SpaceX also struck a deal with Qualcomm to provide terrestrial network infrastructure for Starlink Mobile, as Musk seeks to challenge telecom giants like AT&amp;T and Verizon.

